  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>We know that,</p><p>Total number of three digit number will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>999</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>99</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>900</mn></math>,</p><p>Now,</p><p>Number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;digit number which are divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>900</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>300</mn></math>,</p><p>Number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;digit number which are divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>900</mn><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>225</mn></math>,</p><p>Number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;digit number which are divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#38;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;both&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mfrac><mn>900</mn><mn>12</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>75</mn></math>,</p><p>So , number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;digit number which are divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>225</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>75</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>450</mn></math>,</p><p>Now,&nbsp;number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;digit number which are divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>48</mn></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced open=\"[\" close=\"]\"><mfrac><mn>900</mn><mn>48</mn></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>18</mn></math></p><p>So, number of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></math>&nbsp;digit number which are divisible by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>but&#160;not</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>48</mn></math>&nbsp;will be&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>450</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>432</mn></math></p>"
  }
